    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 5a8be2c9ea162074de1b280235af4bee49551746 -->\nReview at head 5a8be2c9e. Read; the build runs on the pr-test runner (run 44850723830) - the result follows in a later comment.\n\nThe change reads well:\n- The source dropdown now shows \"Selection\" when the operation's source is face or edge picks (src_kind 2). I traced the mapping: the item is only in the list while a pick is already the source, so the dropdown cannot switch a Stock or model source into Selection and cannot queue a phantom edit; a real change still goes through `EditOperationLinks` (Everything Is a Command).\n- `source_dropdown_shows_selection_for_face_and_edge_picks` pins both the AccessKit value (\"the combo shows Selection, displaying queues no edit\") and the undo round-trip for Stock and model sources. Structural assertions, no pixels.\n- The split of `header_rows` into `op_page/header.rs` is the right cure: `op_page.rs` was 489 lines on main and is 351 now; the new module is 144. The moved code is otherwise unchanged (Tool, coolant and #535 rules intact).\n- `docs/decisions/2982-geometry-source.md` is in the PR; the body has `Changelog:` and `Fixes #2982`. No process files, no snapshot PNGs.\n\nClean pending the runner result. Labels: merge-ready, P3 stands; hold the merge until the run is green.\n",
